          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong (co)bordism ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_*=\oplus_{n\geq 0}\Omega_n
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+ring"} graded ring
            whose
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                degree
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                elements are classes of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
                modulo
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
            %li
              %p
                product operation is given by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
                of manifolds;
            %li
              %p
                addition operation is given by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                of manifolds.
          %p
            Instead of bare manifolds one may consider manifolds with extra structure, such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %em oriented cobordism ring
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo *
                          %mi SO
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{SO}_*
            %li
              %p
                the
                %em spin cobordism ring
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo *
                          %mi Spin
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{Spin}_*
          %p etc.
          %p
            In this general context the bare cobordism ring is also denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo *
                    %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^O_*
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo *
                      %mi un
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{un}_*
          %p
            A ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            out of the cobordism ring is a (multiplicative)
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus"} genus
          %p
            More generally, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a fixed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            there is a relative cobordism ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_\bullet(X)
            whose
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                elements are classes modulo cobordism over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                of manifolds equipped with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                (“singular manifolds”);
            %li
              %p
                multiplication of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [f_1 \colon \Sigma_1 \to X]
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [f_2 \colon \Sigma_2 \to X]
                is given by
                %em transversal intersection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_1 \cap_X \Sigma_2
                over
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1
                such
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_1',f_2)
                becomes a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transversal+maps"} transversal maps
                and then form the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_1 \times_{(f_1',f_2)} \Sigma_2
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
          %p
            This product is graded in that it satisfies the
            %strong dimension formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi dim
                  %mi X
                  %mo −
                  %mi dim
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi dim
                  %mi X
                  %mo −
                  %mi dim
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi dim
                  %mi X
                  %mo −
                  %mi dim
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (dim X - dim \Sigma_1) + (dim X - dim \Sigma_2) = dim X - dim (\Sigma_1 \cap_X \Sigma_2)
          %p hence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dim
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi dim
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi dim
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi dim
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  dim (\Sigma_1 \cap_X \Sigma_2 ) = (dim \Sigma_1 + dim \Sigma_2) - dim X
                  \\,.
          %p
            Still more generally, this may be considered for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            being
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds+with+boundary"} manifolds with boundary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega(X,A)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,A)
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+pair"} CW pair
            is the ring of cobordism classes, relative boundary, of singular manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to X
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            lands in in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            The resulting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (X,A) \mapsto \Omega^G_\bullet(X,A)
          %p
            constitutes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology+theory"} generalized homology theory
            (see e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Buchstaber"} Buchstaber, II.8
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+homology+theory"} bordism homology theory
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            that represents this under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
            is the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectra"} Thom spectra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M G
            (e.g.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MO"} MO
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G=O
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"} MU
            for
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = U
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitney+sum"} Whitney sum
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+vector+bundles"} universal vector bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            (this is
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom%27s+theorem"} Thom's theorem
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} M
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega_\bullet^G \simeq \M G_\bullet(\ast) \simeq \pi_\bullet(M G)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This remarkable relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            is known as
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theory"} cobordism theory
            (or “Thom theory”).
          %p
            On general grounds this is equivalently the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology"} generalized cohomology
            of the point (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theory"}> cobordism cohomology theory
            )
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi M
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega_\bullet^G \simeq M G^\bullet(\ast)
          %p
            which justifies calling
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_\bullet^G
            both the “bordism ring” as well as the “cobordism ring”.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToCohomotopy Relation to cohomotopy
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            and let
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \leq n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+construction"} Pontryagin-Thom construction
            induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [X, S^k]
                  \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\Omega^{n-k}(X)
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomotopy"} cohomotopy
            sets of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+group"} cobordism group
            of
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-k)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+manifold"} framing
            up to normally framed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
          %p
            In particular, the natural group structure on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+group"} cobordism group
            (essentially given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            of submanifolds) this way induces a group structure on the cohomotopy sets.
          %p
            This is made explicit for instance in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Kosinski93"} Kosinski 93, chapter IX
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#FramedCobordism Framed cobordism
          %p
            By
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom%27s+theorem"} Thom's theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28B%2Cf%29-structure"} (B,f)-structure
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            (of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi ℬ
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^{\mathcal{B}}_\bullet
                  \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\pi_\bullet(M\mathcal{B})
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
            of manifolds with stable normal
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+of+a+spectrum"} homotopy groups
            of the universal
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
          %p
            Now for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo =
                  %mi Fr
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B} = Fr
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framing"} framing
            structure, then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi Fr
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi 𝕊
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M Fr \simeq \mathbb{S}
          %p
            is equivalently the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom%27s+theorem"} Thom's theorem
            states that there is an isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi fr
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^{fr}_\bullet
                  \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\pi_\bullet(\mathbb{S})
          %p
            between the framed cobordism ring and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} stable homotopy groups of spheres
          %p
            For discussion of computation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(\mathbb{S})
            this way, see for instance (
            %a{:href => "#WangXu10"}> Wang-Xu 10, section 2
            ).
          %p For instance
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 0
                        %mi fr
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{fr}_0 = \mathbb{Z}
                because there are two
                = succeed "-framings" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(O(k)) \simeq \mathbb{Z}_2
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 1
                        %mi fr
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{fr}_1 = \mathbb{Z}_2
                because the only compact connected 1-manifold is the circle, there are two framings on the circle, corresponding to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(O(k)) \simeq \mathbb{Z}_2
                and they are their own negatives.
          %h3#OrientedCobordismRing Oriented cobordism
          #OrientedCobordismOverPoint.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The cobordism ring over the point for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
              manifolds starts out as
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
